{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing","lean:module:QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.trivial_pairFactorised_binding_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.trivial_pairFactorised_binding_zero","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InteractionFactorNotPairwise.lean#L132-L136","doc":"**Non-vacuity.** A pair-factorised interaction exists — the trivial one, `I ≡ 1`, which is the\nindependent (unbound) assembly and indeed has zero binding at every order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.not_pairFactorised_of_b3_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.not_pairFactorised_of_b3_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InteractionFactorNotPairwise.lean#L125-L130","doc":"**The exclusion.** A nonzero measured 3-body cumulant refutes the pair-factorised interaction\nfactor. Since AME2020 gives `b₃ = +1.4262225 ≠ 0`, the interaction amplitude of a cluster is **not**\nthe product of its pairs' interaction amplitudes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.pairFactorised_b4_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.pairFactorised_b4_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InteractionFactorNotPairwise.lean#L120-L123","doc":"**And its 4-body cumulant.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.pairFactorised_b3_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.pairFactorised_b3_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InteractionFactorNotPairwise.lean#L114-L118","doc":"**Hence its 3-body cumulant vanishes identically** — the multiplicative form gains nothing over\nthe additive one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.isPairwise_of_pairFactorised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.isPairwise_of_pairFactorised","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InteractionFactorNotPairwise.lean#L88-L112","doc":"**A pair-factorised interaction gives a pairwise-additive binding.** The product over pairs\nbecomes a sum over bonds under `log`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.bindingFreeEnergy_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.bindingFreeEnergy_mul","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InteractionFactorNotPairwise.lean#L79-L86","doc":"`bindingFreeEnergy` turns a product of positive factors into a sum — the negated\n`freeEnergy_connectedSum`. This is the whole mechanism: the multiplicative structure is a bond sum\nonce the archimedean functor is applied. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.PairFactorised.toBindingMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.PairFactorised.toBindingMap","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InteractionFactorNotPairwise.lean#L67-L73","doc":"The binding map this interaction structure induces, via\n`ArchimedeanTraceBridge.binding_eq_bindingFreeEnergy`: each cluster's binding is `−log` of its\ninteraction factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.PairFactorised.quadI","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.PairFactorised.quadI","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InteractionFactorNotPairwise.lean#L63-L65","doc":"The interaction factor of the four-component assembly: the product over its six pairs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.PairFactorised.tripleI","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.PairFactorised.tripleI","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InteractionFactorNotPairwise.lean#L60-L61","doc":"The interaction factor of the triple `{i,j,k}`: the product over its three pairs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.PairFactorised.pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.PairFactorised.pos","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InteractionFactorNotPairwise.lean#L54-L54","doc":"positivity, discharged for the framework's quantum-integer amplitude class at `q > 1`\n(`ArchimedeanTraceBridge`, `QOU.MathlibExt.qInt_pos`) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.PairFactorised.I","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.PairFactorised.I","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InteractionFactorNotPairwise.lean#L51-L51","doc":"the interaction factor of the pair `{i,j}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.PairFactorised.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.PairFactorised.mk","kind":"ctor","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InteractionFactorNotPairwise.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.PairFactorised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InteractionFactorNotPairwise.PairFactorised","kind":"structure","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InteractionFactorNotPairwise.lean#L46-L54","doc":"An interaction factor assigned **per pair**, with every factor positive so the archimedean\nfunctor `log` is defined on it. A cluster's interaction factor is the product over the pairs it\ncontains — the multiplicative analogue of pair-locality. ","signatureChunk":0}]}